WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:07.280
Throughout the "Halloween" franchise, the timeline&nbsp;
diverges multiple times, and the main series even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.000
features one entry without Michael Myers.&nbsp;
But we're here to help sort through it all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
so grab your favorite carving knife and let's dig&nbsp;
in. This is Michael Myers' backstory explained.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.120
The story of Michael Myers begins on Halloween&nbsp;
night in 1963 in the suburban town of Haddonfield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.280
Illinois, as six-year-old Michael&nbsp;
gets up, walks into his sister's room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.920
and stabs her to death. Michael is sent to&nbsp;
Smith's Grove Sanitarium, where he spends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.960
the rest of his childhood and adolescence.&nbsp;
He is observed and studied by Dr. Sam Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.720
who winds up becoming an expert on the man,&nbsp;
the myth, the legend that is Michael Myers.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.920
On October 30, 1978, the story of Michael&nbsp;
Myers begins in earnest. He escapes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.720
Smith's Grove the night before Halloween&nbsp;
and descends upon Haddonfield. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.920
high schooler Laurie Strode, played by Jamie Lee&nbsp;
Curtis in her first film role, is preparing for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.520
a boring Halloween night babysitting young Tommy&nbsp;
Doyle near the Myers home, which is now abandoned.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.600
Instead of having a dull night earning a little&nbsp;
money on the side, Laurie ends up at the tail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.160
end of Michael's killing spree. After a&nbsp;
night of tracking Michael, Loomis comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.560
to the house where Laurie is fighting him off&nbsp;
and manages to put six bullets in the killer.

00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:26.320
“Halloween II [“two”] picks up later that night,&nbsp;
when Laurie is brought to the Haddonfield Memorial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.080
Hospital, where Michael reappears to finish what&nbsp;
he started. The sequel begins what would become a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.440
major expansion of the "Halloween" lore, by&nbsp;
revealing that Laurie is Michael's sister.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.120
"That girl, that Strode girl.&nbsp;
That's Michael Myers' sister."

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.241
According to "Halloween II," Laurie was extremely&nbsp;
young when Michael killed the rest of his family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.241 --> 00:01:48.800
As a result, she doesn't remember her real family,&nbsp;
and was taken in and raised by the Strodes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.240
This explains why Michael is so dead set on&nbsp;
killing Laurie, as he wants to finish what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.680
he started. "Halloween II" ends with Michael being&nbsp;
presumed dead when there's a fire at the hospital.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.440
The third movie in the franchise, "Halloween&nbsp;
III: Season of the Witch," was an experiment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:11.200
that tried to take the franchise in an anthology&nbsp;
direction, and away from Michael Myers. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:17.120
lukewarm reviews, the series fell into limbo for&nbsp;
years. After it returned with 1988's "Halloween 4:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.960
The Return of Michael Myers," it never again&nbsp;
strayed from the unfeeling killer at its core.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.840
"Halloween 4" stars Danielle Harris as&nbsp;
Jamie Lloyd, Laurie Strode's daughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.800
Jamie is living with a foster family and has&nbsp;
recurring dreams of Michael coming to get her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.480
Those dreams turn out to be warnings when Michael&nbsp;
wakes up from a 10-year coma and goes after his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.760
closest living relative. The movie ends in a&nbsp;
standoff near an abandoned mine, but only after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.680
depicting a moment of psychic connection initially&nbsp;
established via physical contact with Jamie.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.680
In the final moments of "Halloween&nbsp;
4," the family returns home--&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:03:00.400
Jamie eerily wearing a similar costume to the one&nbsp;
Michael wore all the way back in 1963. Just when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.960
everyone thinks they’re safe, Jamie attacks&nbsp;
her foster mother and reappears at the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:10.080
of the stairs holding a bloody pair of scissors.&nbsp;
Dr. Loomis tries to shoot her, but is thwarted.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.680
As "Halloween 5: The Revenge of Michael&nbsp;
Myers" begins, Jamie is mute and in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.000
psychiatric hospital after attempting to kill&nbsp;
her foster mother. This is implied to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.080
result of a moment she shared with Michael&nbsp;
in the previous movie, sparking a connection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:29.280
that leaves Jamie suffering hallucinations that&nbsp;
keep her bond with Michael shrouded in mystery.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.600
In "The Curse of Michael Myers," Michael&nbsp;
returns to his childhood home to kill the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.320
Strode family that now lives there. Tommy Doyle,&nbsp;
now an adult, still lives across the street.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.280
"My name's Tommy. I was only&nbsp;
8 years old when I saw him."

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.280
Doyle has been studying Michael and has&nbsp;
discovered that the root of his evil is an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:54.800
ancient Druid curse known as "Thorn." This&nbsp;
brings the family connection full circle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.840
as the conditions of the curse say the afflicted&nbsp;
must kill their next of kin on Halloween night.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:08.000
Made 20 years after the original, "Halloween H20:&nbsp;
20 Years Later" brought Jamie Lee Curtis back for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:13.680
a story pitched as a direct sequel to "Halloween&nbsp;
II." This movie returns Michael's motivations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.640
to their roots, with him specifically&nbsp;
trying to find and kill Laurie Strode.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:22.880
"H20" brings Michael from Haddonfield to&nbsp;
California, where Laurie has built a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:28.400
identity and life for herself as a schoolteacher.&nbsp;
However, he's foiled again with what looks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:34.320
the most definitive Michael kill yet, when&nbsp;
Laurie chops his head off with a fire axe.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.880
In an unexpected turn, "Halloween: Resurrection"&nbsp;
reveals that the ending of "H20" was an illusion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.920
Of course the decapitated man wasn't Michael.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.640
Instead, Laurie killed an innocent man,&nbsp;
and now has been institutionalized.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.280
"I knew you'd come for me, sooner or later."

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.960
Despite Laurie's best-laid traps, Michael breaks&nbsp;
into the sanitarium where she's being held.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:02.000
She's about to kill him, but begins to grapple&nbsp;
with his mask to make sure it's the real Michael.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:08.560
That doubt gives Michael enough time to stab and&nbsp;
finally kill Laurie, tossing her off the roof.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.880
And that’s only the beginning of Resurrection--&nbsp;
Michael goes on yet another killing spree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.600
aided in part by Busta Rhymes and&nbsp;
Tyra Banks. Yes, you heard that right.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.080
Laurie's death could have been a&nbsp;
huge moment in the "Halloween" canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.320
but it finally left the franchise&nbsp;
nowhere to go but back to the beginning.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:31.840
In 2007, the franchise returned thanks&nbsp;
to Rob Zombie, who directed a remake of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:37.760
the original 1978 Carpenter classic. This&nbsp;
poorly received installment more or less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:43.520
retold the story of the first movie, but many&nbsp;
felt it didn't hold a candle to the original.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:47.760
Zombie followed up his remake with his own&nbsp;
version of "Halloween II." Set two years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.720
after the events in Haddonfield, Laurie begins&nbsp;
having hallucinations in which she sees herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.067
acting out Michael's past murders. The movie&nbsp;
also reveals Laurie to be Michael's sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:58.800
Angel Myers, only at the end of this film, Laurie&nbsp;
manages to actually kill Michael. After stabbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.840
him with his own knife, Laurie puts on his&nbsp;
mask and becomes the new "Michael Myers."

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:08.000
With the 2018 reimagining of&nbsp;
"Halloween," the series went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.400
back to basics, giving viewers a&nbsp;
direct sequel to 1978's "Halloween"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.200
and disregarding the big twist connecting&nbsp;
Laurie and Michael in "Halloween II."

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.720
In this timeline, Michael has been&nbsp;
incarcerated for the past 40 years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:25.120
for the killings he committed in the very&nbsp;
first movie. He breaks out to track down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.960
and kill Laurie, who in this continuity is&nbsp;
definitely not his sister. Over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:37.360
Laurie has become a reclusive alcoholic who's very&nbsp;
good at setting traps for Michael. It pays off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:43.840
because a trap she lays for him sets her house&nbsp;
ablaze, with Michael presumably dead inside. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.120
with sequels "Halloween Kills" and "Halloween&nbsp;
Ends" announced shortly after that movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:55.040
release, it was soon clear that Michael also&nbsp;
survived that fire, and lived to kill again.

